---
description: When to search and save Alexein AI memory
alwaysApply: false
---

Alexein AI holds what the user has chosen to remember across sessions and apps.

- Before answering something that depends on what the user said before (their preferences, projects, people or past
  decisions), call `memory_search`. Open a result with `memory_open` when you need its full text.
- When the user states a lasting fact, preference or decision, save it with `memory_add`, in one short sentence.
- Don't save secrets (passwords, keys, tokens), or one-off chatter that won't matter next time.
- If you're unsure how the user wants memory handled, call `memory_how_they_work`.
